body:
## Environment
- VS Code version: 1.132.0
- Copilot Chat extension version: 0.60.0
- Provider: Custom Endpoint (`vendor: "customendpoint"`), `apiType: "chat-completions"`
- Backend: self-hosted vLLM 0.22.1 (OpenAI-compatible `/v1/chat/completions`, streaming)
- Model tested: `moonshotai/Kimi-K2.6` (reproducible on any model behind this backend)

## Summary
When a Custom Endpoint / BYOK chat-completions model streams a delta chunk that includes an **empty** `tool_calls` array alongside real `content` (e.g. `{"content":" I","tool_calls":[]}`), the response text is silently discarded. The request completes successfully (`finish_reason:"stop"`), output tokens are correctly counted/billed, but the chat UI shows "Sorry, no response was returned" because no text ever reaches the chat view.

## Root cause
In `extensions/copilot/src/platform/networking/node/stream.ts`, `SSEProcessor.processSSEInner()`:

```ts
let handled = true;
if (choice.delta?.tool_calls) {
    // ... StreamingToolCalls.update(choice) — iterates the array, no-op if empty
} else if (/* other cases */) {
    ...
} else {
    handled = false;
}

if (!handled) {
    solution.append(choice); // <-- this reads choice.delta.content
    if (await emitSolution()) { continue; }
}
```

`if (choice.delta?.tool_calls)` only checks **truthiness**. An empty array `[]` is truthy in JavaScript, so this branch is entered even when there are zero actual tool calls. Because the branch is entered, `handled` stays `true` (it's never reset to `false`), so the final `if (!handled) { solution.append(choice); ... }` — the only code path that reads `choice.delta.content` — is skipped. The real text in that delta is dropped.

This repeats on every content-bearing chunk in the stream if the backend attaches `tool_calls: []` to all of them (confirmed via raw curl capture — see below), so 100% of the model's answer text is lost, chunk by chunk, while the model still finishes normally and tokens are still billed.

## Suggested fix
Check for a non-empty array instead of mere presence:

```ts
if (choice.delta?.tool_calls?.length) {
```

## Reproduction
Raw SSE captured directly from the backend for a trivial prompt ("what model are you"), replayed with the exact request VS Code sent (temperature, tools, messages all identical):

```
data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"finish_reason":null}], ...}
data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning":" The"},"finish_reason":null}], ...}
... (reasoning deltas omitted) ...
data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":" I","tool_calls":[]},"finish_reason":null}], ...}
data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":" am","tool_calls":[]},"finish_reason":null}], ...}
data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":" using","tool_calls":[]},"finish_reason":null}], ...}
...
data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"**.","tool_calls":[]},"finish_reason":null}], ...}
data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{},"finish_reason":"stop"}], ...}
data: [DONE]
```

- `system_fingerprint: vllm-0.22.1-tp8-327f7987`
- The reasoning field is delivered as `delta.reasoning` (not `reasoning_content`), which is a separate (correctly handled) quirk.
- Sending the identical request directly via `curl`/Node `https` against the backend reproduces this SSE shape 100% of the time (6/6 test runs).
- A local proxy that strips the empty `tool_calls` key from delta chunks before they reach VS Code fully resolves the issue, confirming the root cause above.

## How other clients handle this (comparison)
The AI SDK's `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` provider (used by Opencode and others) does not have this issue, because it checks `content`, `reasoning`, and `tool_calls` as **independent, sequential conditions** on each delta, rather than routing the whole chunk through one mutually-exclusive branch with a shared "handled" flag:

```ts
// simplified from openai-compatible-chat-language-model.ts doStream()
if (delta.content) {
  controller.enqueue({ type: 'text-delta', delta: delta.content });
}
if (delta.tool_calls != null) {
  for (const toolCallDelta of delta.tool_calls) {
    processToolCallDelta(toolCallDelta); // no-op on an empty array
  }
}
```

Both checks always run. An empty `tool_calls` array just produces a zero-iteration loop — it never gates or suppresses the `content` branch. This confirms the suggested fix (`choice.delta?.tool_calls?.length` instead of `choice.delta?.tool_calls`) brings VS Code's parser in line with how comparable OpenAI-compatible streaming clients already handle this exact backend behavior.

## Impact
Any BYOK/Custom Endpoint chat-completions model behind a backend that includes an empty `tool_calls` array on content deltas (observed with vLLM 0.22.1) will silently fail in VS Code Copilot Chat — the model answers correctly and is billed, but the user sees no response at all. Other tools that guard with `tool_calls.length` (or iterate an array and no-op on empty) are unaffected by this same backend behavior.
